  speakerName: Rayo
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'After all that walking, you''ll probably be hungry!

    In Ilokano,
    ''mangan'' means ''eat.''

    It is an action verb used when talking about the
    act of eating.

    For example, when it''s time for lunch, you can say ''mangan.''

    Listen
    carefully: mangan.

    Now, try saying ''mangan'' yourself.'
